1.1 Product Overview - Context diagrams
LearnUP is a B2B multi-tenant online learning and corporate training platform. The context diagrams show the system boundary and everything outside it: the five actor roles and the four external systems named in the use case list (167 use cases), with the data that flows between them and LearnUP.
Figure 1 gives the overview. Because it would be too crowded to show every flow on one picture, Figures 2 to 5 detail the flows of each actor group, and Figure 6 shows what is exchanged with each external system.
External entities - actors
#EntityDescription1GuestIndividual representing an outside organization who does not have an account yet. Views subscription plans, registers an Organization, makes the mock payment, asks for the registration link again and verifies the email to activate the Organizer account.2OrganizerTraining administrator of an Organization (one Organizer at a time). Manages the Subscription, organization information, Instructor and Learner accounts; approves Courses; assigns training; handles reports at Organization level; views and exports reports and the organization logs.3InstructorPerson in charge of training content. Builds and manages Courses, Modules, Lessons, materials and assessments; submits Courses for approval; grades and finalizes results; creates new Course versions and releases the assets of old ones.4LearnerEmployee who takes part in training. Joins assigned and elective Courses, learns, takes Quizzes and Assignments, performs peer review, receives Certificates and completes the training evaluation form.5AdminPlatform administrator. Manages Subscription Plans, platform parameters, Organizations and their Subscription status; handles escalated reports; suspends and unsuspends Organizations; replaces an Organizer; views the platform logs.External entities - systems
#EntityDescription6Email ServiceSends email: account invitations, links to reopen a registration for payment, email verification links, password recovery links and system notifications. Used by 32 use cases.7Mock Payment ServiceSimulated payment service that processes the transactions of registering, renewing and upgrading a Subscription. Used by 4 use cases.8Media Storage ServiceStores and serves files: Video and Reading materials, Course covers, Organization logos, submission files, Assignment prompt files and exported reports. Used by 20 use cases.9Google Identity ServiceGoogle's identity service, used to verify the identity of a user who signs in with a Google account (UC-05.1).Note: the architecture document treats physical file storage as infrastructure and merges email delivery into the Notification Service. The use case list still names them as external actors, so the diagrams follow the use case list.
